  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5455",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the biological pathway leading to the target SBC-5 through multiple independent routes. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets SBC-5. This indicates a shared biochemical mechanism involving the enzyme 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which is likely a key mediator in the interaction between Mollicellin N and SBC-5. The presence of multiple distinct targets for Mollicellin N, including A704 and Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5, further supports the idea that it may interact with different molecular players in the same pathway. The integration of these pathways suggests that Mollicellin N may modulate the activity of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which then influences SBC-5. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link between Mollicellin N and SBC-5, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
